According to Section II. Potential Red Flags in Deposits of Securities, a red flag arises when a customer deposits physical share certificates or electronically deposits shares issued by a company that:  
- Is a shell company;  
- Has no apparent business, revenues, or products;  
- Has SEC filings that are not current, incomplete, or nonexistent;  
- Has undergone several recent name changes or business combinations/recapitalizations;  
- Has been the subject of a prior trading suspension; or  
- Has officers or insiders with a history of regulatory or criminal violations, or are associated with multiple low-priced stock issuers.  

(Refer to Section II. Potential Red Flags in Deposits of Securities.)
